{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_5480",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the development of Contact Dermatitis through a series of indirect pathways involving other drugs. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone is linked to Discoid Lupus Erythematosus, a condition that in turn is associated with Prednicarbate and Desoximetasone, both of which are indicated to cause Contact Dermatitis. This indicates a potential mechanism where Prednisolone, through its metabolites or related compounds, may contribute to the pathogenesis of Contact Dermatitis. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Prednisolone to Contact Dermatitis highlights a possible role in inflammatory or immune-mediated skin disorders. The integration of these pathways suggests that Prednisolone may act as a mediator in the development of Contact Dermatitis, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
